1.0.2

Documentation refresh from package 1.0.1, prepared 2026-11-18; not a publication record.
Upstream reviewed: Microsoft Go sqlcmd v1.10.0 -> v1.11.0.
Authoritative release: https://github.com/microsoft/go-sqlcmd/releases/tag/v1.11.0
Immutable source: https://github.com/microsoft/go-sqlcmd/tree/a97013a80b01f3aaac4fb17e9ef422283f15cb2f
Release changes: https://github.com/microsoft/go-sqlcmd/blob/a97013a80b01f3aaac4fb17e9ef422283f15cb2f/CHANGELOG.md

Added a selective diagnostics reference for --ascii table output and -j raw-error
prefix preservation (Go sqlcmd 1.11.0 minimum), YAML config suffix validation,
-G without a username selecting ActiveDirectoryDefault, and the token-auth fix
that supplies the previously missing password/token in the internal connection URL.
Clarified -F certificate-hostname semantics and delimiter output versus quoted CSV.
Kept explicit authentication gates and password nonexposure; no blanket client
version uplift. SQL scripts, security documents, tests, and builder are unchanged.
Azure SQL Edge removal needs no operator guidance change: this package did not
claim Edge provisioning support. Devcontainer, dependencies/toolchain, translations,
CI/release infrastructure, and empty-argument panic fixes add no diagnostic workflow.

Evidence is source-backed only. The supplied official release snapshot has no
assets; no official binary/help capture, upstream build, or sqlcmd/SQL Server runtime
validation was performed. The existing merged-skill builder omits references and
SQL scripts; selective installation must retain the diagnostics references directory.
